[ti:The Last Rose of Summer]
[ar:Traditional]
[00:00.00]Tis the last rose of summer, left blooming alone
[00:30.00]All her lovely companions are faded and gone
[01:00.00]No flower of her kindred, no rosebud is nigh
[01:30.00]To reflect back her blushes or give sigh for sigh
[02:00.00]I'll not leave thee, thou lone one, to pine on the stem
[02:30.00]Since the lovely are sleeping, go sleep thou with them
[02:30.67]Thus kindly I scatter thy leaves o'er the bed
[02:31.33]Where thy mates of the garden lie scentless and dead
